<title>UK: Warsaw bourse slip a buying opportunity - Merrill.</title>
<headline>Warsaw bourse slip a buying opportunity - Merrill.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A slide in Poland's WIG index from a year high of 15,078.7 points to 13,498 represents a buying opportunity for investors looking to the medium and long term, Merrill Lynch first vice president Dan Lubash said in a research note.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that the market has overcorrected. While a recent parliamentary move to reduce nex year's income tax levels raises concerns about 1997 inflation targets, Poland remains a growth leader in eastern Europe,&quot; Lubash said.</p>
<p>He recommends domestic consumption plays such as food producer Agros, tyremaker Debica and paint maker Polifarb Ciezsyn.</p>
<p>As well as BIG bank, which Merrill raised to a buy earlier this week, Lubash also recommends Elektrim.</p>
<p>-- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
